<LegalPage eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy Policy" description="What Vector stores locally, what billing requires, and what connected providers receive.">
  <section><h2>Local and Builder workspaces</h2><p>Vector Desktop is designed to keep repositories, local sessions, preferences, and checkpoints on your computer. Vector Builder creates a separate cloud project and isolated runtime for each build. Builder files, conversation history, logs, diffs, previews, usage, and messages are retained until you remove the project or Vector applies its published retention policy.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Accounts and platform data</h2><p>Vector accounts use Supabase Auth. Vector stores your account identifier, email, display profile, subscription entitlement, Builder project and run metadata, usage records, paired-device settings, and configured tool metadata. Saved provider and connection credentials are encrypted at rest with a server-managed application key.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Builder execution</h2><p>Vector uses Vercel infrastructure for the website, server functions, scheduled reconciliation, and isolated Builder sandboxes. Project files, prompts, command output, and tool results are processed there. Model requests are sent to the model provider selected for the build. Vector does not place unrelated platform credentials inside customer-controlled sandboxes.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Model and tool providers</h2><p>Prompts, selected files, tool results, or other context may be sent to the model and integration providers you choose. Their privacy policies apply. Vector does not centrally store your model API keys as part of the license service.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Billing and license data</h2><p>Stripe processes payment details. Vector receives and stores the billing email, Stripe customer and subscription identifiers, subscription status, renewal state, license metadata, a hashed activation token, a one-way device identifier, device name/platform, and recent verification timestamps. Vector does not receive your full card number.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Purchase email</h2><p>Resend delivers the purchase confirmation and license key. The message contains your billing email, license key, expiration date, and purchase link. Resend processes that delivery under its own privacy terms.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Diagnostics</h2><p>Some Vector builds may use Sentry for crash diagnostics. Diagnostic reports can include application version, operating system, stack traces, and technical state. Vector does not intentionally attach repository files to crash reports.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Paired computer actions</h2><p>Builder can reach a paired Vector Desktop only when you connect that computer, select its tool for a build, and enable the required browser or terminal permission. Requested actions are delivered to the paired app for local visibility and approval. You can disable either permission or disconnect the computer from Settings.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Security and retention</h2><p>Activation tokens are stored locally in a restricted application file. Server-side records store hashes rather than plaintext activation tokens. Billing, account, Builder, connection, and license records are retained as needed to provide access, recover projects, prevent abuse, resolve disputes, and satisfy legal obligations. Deleting a Builder workspace removes its isolated runtime before Vector removes the database record.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can disconnect providers, remove local data, cancel renewal, and deactivate a computer from Vector. For billing or privacy requests, contact <a href="mailto:contact.astr0gpt@gmail.com">contact.astr0gpt@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
</LegalPage>
